Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Graph convolutional regression of cardiac depolarization", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"1351ea7e-cffc-8a44-b369-1125d7d384ac"],

Cell["\<\
Phases 1-2: equation reference and deterministic synthetic evidence\
\>", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"68e823b0-e45d-c747-b24e-ef53e47a31da"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Scope and evidence", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"9e1e5994-3746-cc4f-bcc3-97ac707e33e2"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook implements paper equations and a synthetic graph-wavefront \
demonstrator. It does not reproduce the unavailable trained 20-layer network \
or clinical experiments.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"27bce0f9-b5f6-0f42-817a-ef4508e4e251"],

Cell["\<\
Loads the HeartGCNModel` package from src/HeartGCNModel.wl after fixing the \
RNG seed to 42 so every equation check and synthetic experiment is \
deterministic.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"28e39edc-aca8-9d4b-8887-67d4fe67f5e1"],

Cell["\<\
SeedRandom[42]; Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"src\", \
\"HeartGCNModel.wl\"}]]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:=",ExpressionUUID->"c03a15cd-835a-b042-96f6-f05472edeb40"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Equation checks", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"9f5f481e-887e-9546-b756-bbd6af7f35c5"],

Cell["\<\
MeanSAGEAggregate[neighbors] returns the componentwise mean of the neighbor \
feature vectors. If the neighborhood is empty, it returns a zero vector when \
an explicit Dimension option is given, otherwise \
Missing[\"EmptyNeighborhood\"]. This is the mean GraphSAGE aggregate h_N(i) = \
mean(h_j, j in N(i)) (claim C1, Method pp. 2-3).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f793715e-13ad-c346-9f86-4637e40f9640"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["MeanSAGEAggregate[{{1, 2}, {3, 4}}]", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:=",ExpressionUUID->"11507e8e-7b50-614c-8ddb-b73b315722b9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"2", ",", "3"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.993439635105301*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[4]=",ExpressionUUID->"8422f59f-5e62-6143-ba20-0ce4663e99ef"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
GraphSAGEUpdate[self, neighborhood, parameters] applies the paper's vertex \
update h'_i = sigma(W_i h_i + b_i + W_N a_i + b_N), with weights shared over \
all vertices, then the activation (default leaky ReLU). This is claim C2 \
(Method, p. 3).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fa6fd555-ff17-9a47-9107-52c5ae4541a4"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
p = <|\"SelfWeights\" -> IdentityMatrix[2], \"SelfBias\" -> {0, 0}, \
\"NeighborWeights\" -> IdentityMatrix[2], \"NeighborBias\" -> {0, 0}, \
\"Activation\" -> Identity|>; GraphSAGEUpdate[{1, 2}, {{3, 4}, {5, 6}}, p]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a932f64e-2897-b54f-9ec6-28ae902a47d3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"5", ",", "7"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.993439635120903*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[5]=",ExpressionUUID->"91ab7f07-cd5b-9341-b01b-4000c0c5297e"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
WeightedLATMSE[prediction, truth, measuredMask] computes the LAT loss (1/N) \
Sum alpha_i (prediction_i - truth_i)^2 with alpha = 2 at measured vertices \
and 1 elsewhere (claim C3, p. 3). QRSDuration[times] = Max[times] - \
Min[times]. CombinedLoss returns <|LATLoss, QRSLoss, TotalLoss|> with \
TotalLoss = L_LAT + (QRS(prediction) - QRS(truth))^2 (claim C4, p. 3).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"768e3be4-28bc-5441-b4a7-5cbc997a47d4"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
{WeightedLATMSE[{1, 2}, {0, 0}, {True, False}], CombinedLoss[{1, 3}, {1, 2}, \
{True, False}]} \
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:=",ExpressionUUID->"18e69f63-bbf5-bc40-a000-67079f6e5fae"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"3", ",", 
   RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\<\"LATLoss\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
      FractionBox["1", "2"]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"QRSLoss\"\>", "\[Rule]", "1"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"TotalLoss\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
      FractionBox["3", "2"]}]}], "\[RightAssociation]"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.993439635139023*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[6]=",ExpressionUUID->"7ad9670f-4b2b-2f4e-9e6d-1bef77ba56f2"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
AnisotropyTensor[f, r] builds the anisotropy matrix D = (1-r) f f^T + r \
IdentityMatrix with default r = 1/3; the fiber f is normalized and must be \
nonzero. VirtualEdgeLength[e, f, r] = Sqrt[e . D . e]. EdgeTravelTime[length, \
speed] = length / speed for positive speed and Infinity for zero speed, so \
scar edges are impassable (issue I7). These reproduce claim C5 (Data \
Generation, p. 5).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"42e0b281-a660-1849-80f5-3d735e419557"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
{AnisotropyTensor[{1, 0, 0}], VirtualEdgeLength[{2, 0, 0}, {1, 0, 0}], \
VirtualEdgeLength[{0, 3, 0}, {1, 0, 0}], EdgeTravelTime[6, 3]}\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:=",ExpressionUUID->"9bc81392-79aa-f541-9f3b-12fc6dc01c97"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", 
       FractionBox["1", "3"], ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", 
       FractionBox["1", "3"]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", "2", ",", 
   SqrtBox["3"], ",", "2"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.993439635143532*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[7]=",ExpressionUUID->"b860fb33-fac9-3644-8041-ace0795657a1"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Synthetic wavefront", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0d3ea0c9-8b6a-0846-a029-ac695d0008bb"],

Cell["\<\
SyntheticWavefront[spec] builds a deterministic rectangular unit-edge grid \
graph and computes ground-truth activation times as shortest-path distances \
from a single source. This demonstrates claim C6: activation follows shortest \
paths from activation points (Data Generation, p. 5). The grid is not cardiac \
anatomy and speed is uniform.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"81a6b908-b84f-b64b-a9c2-1e74366d51e2"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
experiment = SyntheticWavefront[]; Graph[experiment[\"Graph\"], \
VertexCoordinates -> experiment[\"Coordinates\"], VertexStyle -> \
Thread[Range[Length[experiment[\"Truth\"]]] -> (ColorData[\"TemperatureMap\"] \
/@ Rescale[experiment[\"Truth\"]])], ImageSize -> Large]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:=",ExpressionUUID->"0d3aea9e-d441-bc4e-9db6-54682897c8e6"],

